---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const contactEmail = 'invest@southvillagedev.com';

const work = [
  { src: '/images/infill.jpg',           alt: 'Modern infill home with rooftop deck, Indianapolis',          cap: 'Modern infill with rooftop deck, Indianapolis' },
  { src: '/images/modern201.jpg',        alt: 'Contemporary new-build home with rooftop deck, Indianapolis', cap: 'Contemporary new build, sold' },
  { src: '/images/rebuild-progress.jpg', alt: 'Craftsman bungalow rebuild in progress on a city lot',        cap: 'Craftsman rebuild in progress, near south side' },
  { src: '/images/farmhouse.jpg',        alt: 'Modern farmhouse new construction nearing completion',        cap: 'Ground-up modern farmhouse, final stretch' },
  { src: '/images/suburban.jpg',         alt: 'Two-story home, suburban new construction',                   cap: 'Suburban ground-up two-story, delivered' },
  { src: '/images/crew.jpg',             alt: 'Crews laying brick and finishing a new build',                cap: 'Our crews at work, brick and finish stage' },
  { src: '/images/interior.jpg',         alt: 'Finished bathroom with hexagonal tile shower',                cap: 'Interior finish standard' },
  { src: '/images/multifam.jpg',         alt: 'Three-story multifamily building with balconies',             cap: 'Multifamily experience: three-story garden apartments' },
  { src: '/images/render.jpg',           alt: 'Rendering of planned four-unit multifamily product',          cap: 'Pipeline product rendering' },
];

const timeline = [
  { when: 'Now – 2026',     what: 'Phase 1A production begins.', detail: 'Continuous single-family builds across five submarkets; first closings inside year one. Madison assemblage secured at pre-re-rate basis.' },
  { when: '2026 – 2028',    what: 'Rezone window.',              detail: 'A 14 to 20 month target; the comp-plan designation converts the rezone from plan amendment to plan execution.' },
  { when: '2027',           what: 'Road diet Phase 2 complete.', detail: 'The corridor fronting The Madison Project is fully delivered.' },
  { when: 'Winter 2028',    what: 'Road diet Phase 3 (earliest).', detail: 'Corridor holds re-rate; hold parcels release into the pipeline.' },
  { when: '2028 +',         what: 'Madison vertical construction.', detail: 'Begins immediately on rezone approval, with no infrastructure wait.' },
  { when: '2029 – 2030 +',  what: 'District delivery.',          detail: 'Madison stabilization and corridor positions capture the follow-on re-rate.' },
];
---
<Base>

<nav>
  <a class="mark" href="#top"><img src="/images/logo-mark-light.png" alt="" />South Village</a>
  <div class="links">
    <a href="#moment">The moment</a>
    <a href="#program">The program</a>
    <a href="#work">Built work</a>
    <a href="#team">Principals</a>
    <a href="#contact">Inquire</a>
  </div>
</nav>

<header id="top">
  <div class="hero-inner">
    <p class="intro">South Village Development · Indianapolis, Indiana</p>
    <h1>The near south side is re&#8209;pricing. We build ahead of it.</h1>
    <p class="sub">A neighborhood-scale development program on the Madison Avenue corridor, led by a builder who has spent his life on the south side and timed to $47 million of city infrastructure already underway.</p>
  </div>
  <figure class="hero-photo">
    <img src="/images/hero.jpg" alt="Completed craftsman rebuild on the near south side of Indianapolis" fetchpriority="high" />
    <figcaption>Full rebuild on the near south side, delivered</figcaption>
  </figure>
</header>

<section id="moment">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="kicker">Why now</p>
    <h2>The city is executing its own plan. We are building inside it.</h2>
    <div class="rule"></div>
    <div class="cols">
      <div>
        <p>Three conditions overlap on the near south side right now. The Madison Avenue Road Diet and the Interurban Trail, $47 million of funded public infrastructure, are under construction. Institutional projects are breaking ground blocks away. And pricing has not yet re-rated: the surrounding market still trades at a fraction of what new construction commands one neighborhood north.</p>
        <p>In Bates-Hendricks, new builds close above $400,000 while the near-south median sits in the mid-$250s. That spread is the opportunity, and it narrows as the corridor delivers.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>The funded Red Line extension runs directly down Madison Avenue. A 2024 Indiana Association of Realtors study documents a walkability premium of up to 27%, a premium this corridor does not yet price in, and will.</p>
        <p>The program does not depend on a rezoning fight or a speculative masterplan. The city's comprehensive plan already designates the corridor for what we intend to build. Our work is execution of a public plan, on private land, ahead of the re-rate.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="figures">
      <div>
        <div class="n">$47M</div>
        <div class="d">Funded city infrastructure, road diet and trail, under construction on the corridor</div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="n">~$150K</div>
        <div class="d">Gap between the near-south median and new-construction pricing one neighborhood north</div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="n">27%</div>
        <div class="d">Documented walkability premium, 2024 Indiana Association of Realtors study</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="map">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 900 700" role="img" aria-label="Illustrative diagram of the Madison Avenue corridor showing the three road diet phases, the Interurban Trail, surrounding neighborhoods, and the Madison Project site">
        <!-- neighborhood fields -->
        <rect x="150" y="70"  width="240" height="110" rx="6" fill="#242B25" opacity="0.055"/>
        <text x="270" y="130" text-anchor="middle" font-size="17" font-style="italic" fill="#43423A">Old Southside</text>
        <rect x="520" y="100" width="215" height="280" rx="6" fill="#242B25" opacity="0.055"/>
        <text x="627" y="245" text-anchor="middle" font-size="17" font-style="italic" fill="#43423A">Bates-Hendricks</text>
        <rect x="150" y="235" width="240" height="215" rx="6" fill="#8A3D2C" opacity="0.07"/>
        <text x="270" y="300" text-anchor="middle" font-size="17" font-style="italic" fill="#6C3022">South Village</text>
        <rect x="520" y="480" width="215" height="100" rx="6" fill="#242B25" opacity="0.055"/>
        <text x="627" y="535" text-anchor="middle" font-size="17" font-style="italic" fill="#43423A">Garfield Park</text>

        <!-- cross streets -->
        <g stroke="#C9C6B8" stroke-width="1.5">
          <line x1="130" y1="210" x2="790" y2="210"/>
          <line x1="130" y1="400" x2="790" y2="400"/>
          <line x1="130" y1="470" x2="790" y2="470"/>
          <line x1="130" y1="585" x2="790" y2="585"/>
        </g>
        <g font-size="12.5" font-style="italic" fill="#8B8A7D">
          <text x="790" y="204" text-anchor="end">Morris St</text>
          <text x="790" y="394" text-anchor="end">Pleasant Run Pkwy</text>
          <text x="700" y="464" text-anchor="end">Raymond St</text>
          <text x="790" y="579" text-anchor="end">Southern Ave</text>
        </g>

        <!-- Shelby St -->
        <line x1="745" y1="240" x2="745" y2="600" stroke="#C9C6B8" stroke-width="1.5"/>
        <text x="760" y="430" font-size="12.5" font-style="italic" fill="#8B8A7D" transform="rotate(90 760 430)">Shelby St</text>

        <!-- Interurban Trail -->
        <line x1="482" y1="90" x2="482" y2="600" stroke="#8A3D2C" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-dasharray="2 7" stroke-linecap="round"/>
        <text x="498" y="268" font-size="12.5" font-style="italic" fill="#8A3D2C" transform="rotate(90 498 268)">Interurban Trail (funded)</text>

        <!-- Madison Ave spine, phased -->
        <line x1="455" y1="40"  x2="455" y2="400" stroke="#242B25" stroke-width="13" stroke-linecap="round"/>
        <line x1="455" y1="400" x2="455" y2="500" stroke="#8A3D2C" stroke-width="13"/>
        <line x1="455" y1="500" x2="455" y2="620" stroke="#A8A79A" stroke-width="13" stroke-dasharray="14 10" stroke-linecap="round"/>
        <text x="438" y="138" font-size="14.5" fill="#26261F" letter-spacing=".04em" transform="rotate(-90 438 138)" text-anchor="middle">MADISON AVENUE</text>

        <!-- endpoints -->
        <circle cx="455" cy="40" r="5.5" fill="#242B25"/>
        <text x="455" y="24" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13.5" font-style="italic" fill="#43423A">to Fountain Square &amp; Downtown</text>
        <text x="473" y="46" font-size="12" font-style="italic" fill="#8B8A7D">Ray St</text>
        <text x="455" y="646" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13.5" font-style="italic" fill="#43423A">corridor continues south to Troy &amp; Hanna Ave</text>

        <!-- Madison Project marker -->
        <rect x="430" y="415" width="22" height="22" fill="#F1EFE8" stroke="#8A3D2C" stroke-width="2.5"/>
        <line x1="430" y1="426" x2="330" y2="426" stroke="#8A3D2C" stroke-width="1.2"/>
        <text x="324" y="421" text-anchor="end" font-size="14.5" fill="#6C3022">The Madison Project</text>
        <text x="324" y="438" text-anchor="end" font-size="12" font-style="italic" fill="#8B8A7D">mixed-use anchor site</text>

        <!-- legend -->
        <g font-size="13" fill="#43423A">
          <line x1="140" y1="684" x2="176" y2="684" stroke="#242B25" stroke-width="9" stroke-linecap="round"/>
          <text x="186" y="689">Road diet Phase 1: Ray St to Pleasant Run, underway</text>
          <line x1="492" y1="684" x2="528" y2="684" stroke="#8A3D2C" stroke-width="9"/>
          <text x="538" y="689">Phase 2: 2027</text>
          <line x1="660" y1="684" x2="696" y2="684" stroke="#A8A79A" stroke-width="9" stroke-dasharray="11 8" stroke-linecap="round"/>
          <text x="706" y="689">Phase 3: winter 2028</text>
        </g>
      </svg>
      <p class="mapnote">Illustrative diagram of the corridor: schematic, not to scale, phase limits approximate. $47M road diet and trail per City of Indianapolis DPW; phase timing per public project schedule.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="dark" id="program">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="kicker">The program</p>
    <h2>An engine, an anchor, and the corridor itself.</h2>
    <div class="rule"></div>
    <div class="phases">
      <div class="phase">
        <div class="tag">Phase 1A</div>
        <div>
          <h3>The single-family engine</h3>
          <p>Ten to fifteen homes per year, throttled to absorption, across five proven near-south submarkets. Proven comps in Bates-Hendricks and Old Southside, deliberate comp-setting in South Village, and volume product on Shelby. The engine produces closings and distributions from year one. It does not wait on any other phase.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="phase">
        <div class="tag">Phase 1B</div>
        <div>
          <h3>The Madison Project</h3>
          <p>A mixed-use anchor development on an industrial assemblage the city's comprehensive plan already designates for exactly this use, making the rezone plan execution rather than a plan amendment. Ten-year tax abatement eligibility is confirmed. Vertical construction begins on approval, with no infrastructure wait.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="phase">
        <div class="tag">Phase 1C</div>
        <div>
          <h3>Corridor positions</h3>
          <p>Land control along Madison Avenue held through the final phase of the road diet. As the corridor delivers, these positions release into the pipeline, capturing the re-rate the first two phases help create.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="band">
  <img src="/images/church.jpg" alt="Historic brick church tower on the near south side under restoration" loading="lazy" />
  <div class="cap">
    <p class="kicker">The fabric</p>
    <p>The near south side was built once, and built well: brick churches, craftsman blocks, streetcar lots. Our work restores that fabric and adds to it, rather than replacing it.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<section id="work">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="kicker">Built work</p>
    <h2>The operator is not theoretical.</h2>
    <div class="rule"></div>
    <div class="cols">
      <p>South Village is led on the ground by a builder with more than a decade of construction and development on the south side: thirty-plus homes delivered and over $17 million in real estate assets created across Indianapolis, Trafalgar, New Palestine, and Bloomington. Historic rebuilds, modern infill, suburban ground-up, multifamily.</p>
      <p>Every photograph below is our own work. We publish it because an investor's first diligence question should already be answered on this page: yes, this team builds, finishes, and closes.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      {work.map((w) => (
        <figure>
          <img src={w.src} alt={w.alt} loading="lazy" />
          <figcaption>{w.cap}</figcaption>
        </figure>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="team" style="padding-top:0">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="kicker">Principals</p>
    <h2>Three principals. One operating system.</h2>
    <div class="rule"></div>
    <div class="team">
      <div>
        <img src="/images/gabe.jpg" alt="Portrait of Gabriel Lopez" loading="lazy" />
        <h3>Gabriel Lopez</h3>
        <p class="role">Operating Partner, Construction &amp; Development</p>
        <p>A lifelong south-sider and president of Escanor Capital Investments. More than a decade building on the south side: 30+ homes, $17M+ in assets created. Gabe runs land, crews, product, and delivery.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="ph">CA</div>
        <h3>Cruz Arboneaux</h3>
        <p class="role">Operating Partner, Research &amp; Underwriting</p>
        <p>A Marine Corps veteran and the program's underwriter. Cruz built the research the program is sequenced against: parcel-level acquisition mapping, infrastructure timing, comp bands, absorption discipline. Every acquisition is gated against it.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <img src="/images/matthew.jpg" alt="Portrait of Matthew Durnya" loading="lazy" />
        <h3>Matthew Durnya</h3>
        <p class="role">Principal, Capital Markets &amp; Investor Relations</p>
        <p>An entrepreneur and brand builder based in Palm Beach, Florida. Matthew owns the program's capital partnerships end to end, from first conversation through closing, and remains each partner's ongoing point of contact. He also leads the program's brand and communications.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section style="padding-top:0">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="kicker">Sequence</p>
    <h2>Sequenced, not speculative.</h2>
    <div class="rule"></div>
    <div class="timeline">
      {timeline.map((t) => (
        <div class="trow">
          <div class="when">{t.when}</div>
          <p><b>{t.what}</b> {t.detail}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
    <p class="tfoot">Phase 1A cash flows do not wait on any of the above. The engine runs from day one.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="invite" id="contact">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="kicker">For qualified investors</p>
    <h2>Request the confidential program overview.</h2>
    <div class="rule"></div>
    <p>Deal-level materials, including economics, structure, and diligence files, are shared privately with qualified investors following an introductory conversation with the principals. We keep the capital partner group deliberately small.</p>
    <a class="btn" href={`mailto:${contactEmail}?subject=Program%20overview%20request`}>Request the overview</a>
    <p class="alt">Or write to us directly at <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a></p>
  </div>
</section>

<footer>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="frow">
      <div><img class="fmark" src="/images/logo-mark-light.png" alt="South Village logo" /><div class="mark">South Village Development LLC</div></div>
      <div>Indianapolis, Indiana</div>
    </div>
    <p class="legal">This website is for informational purposes only and does not constitute an offer to sell, or a solicitation of an offer to buy, any security. Any such offer or solicitation will be made only to qualified investors through definitive offering documents, and only in jurisdictions where permitted by law. Past performance is not indicative of future results. Market figures cited reflect third-party and public sources believed reliable but not independently verified. © South Village Development LLC.</p>
    <p class="legal"><a href="/privacy" style="color:inherit;text-decoration:underline">Privacy Policy</a> · Built by <a href="https://growpalmbeach.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color:inherit;text-decoration:underline">Grow Palm Beach</a></p>
  </div>
</footer>

</Base>
